      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "markdown": "How should the public API handle rate limits?\nKeep it simple."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "role": "assistant",
      "time": "2026-09-21T10:14:31.000Z",
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "thinking",
          "label": "Thought process",
          "text": "The question is about client-facing behaviour rather than server enforcement, so the useful answer covers the response shape and what a caller should do with it. Worth checking what the docs already say before answering.",
          "expanded": true
        },
        {
          "type": "tools",
          "label": "Used a tool",
          "calls": [
            {
              "name": "search_docs",
              "group": "Used a tool",
              "expanded": true,
              "hidden": false,
              "payloads": [
                {
                  "label": "Request",
                  "lang": "json",
                  "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"rate limits\",\n  \"limit\": 5\n}"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Response",
                  "lang": "json",
                  "text": "{\n  \"results\": 3,\n  \"top\": \"429 backoff\",\n  \"sections\": [\"limits\", \"retry\", \"quotas\"]\n}"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "markdown": "Return `429` with a `Retry-After` header and let the client back off.\n\nThree things worth deciding up front:\n\n- Whether limits are per key or per endpoint\n- What the window is, and whether it slides\n- Whether a burst allowance exists\n\nThe header is the part clients actually need — without it they guess, and guessing means retry storms."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "role": "user",
      "time": "2026-09-21T10:16:45.000Z",
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "markdown": "What about a per-endpoint override?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "role": "assistant",
      "time": "2026-09-21T10:17:02.000Z",
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "tools",
          "label": "Used a tool",
          "calls": [
            {
              "name": "get_config",
              "group": "Used a tool",
              "expanded": true,
              "hidden": false,
              "payloads": [
                {
                  "label": "Request",
                  "lang": "json",
                  "text": "{\n  \"section\": \"limits\"\n}"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Response",
                  "lang": "json",
                  "text": "{\n  \"default_rpm\": 60,\n  \"overrides\": {\n    \"/export\": 10\n  }\n}"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "markdown": "Overrides are already supported — `/export` sits at 10 requests a minute against a default of 60.\n\nDocument the override in the endpoint's own reference rather than only in the limits page, or nobody finds it until they hit it."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
